\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Behold! a stranger at the door!
\par He gently knocks, has knocked before:
\par Has waited long, is waiting still:
\par You treat no other friend so ill.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. But will He prove a friend indeed?
\par He will; the very Friend you need:
\par The Man of Nazareth, 'tis He,
\par With garments dyed at Calvary.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Admit Him, for the human breast
\par Ne'er entertained so kind a guest;
\par No mortal tongue their joys can tell
\par With whom He condescends to dwell.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Yet know, nor of the terms complain,
\par Where Jesus comes, He comes to reign;
\par To reign, and with no partial sway;
\par Thoughts must be slain that disobey.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Sovereign of souls! Thou Prince of Peace
\par O may Thy gentle reign increase!
\par Throw wide the door each willing mind;
\par And be His empire all mankind.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

